Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Name the helper archive in the C module map

COpenCombineHelpers is the module that declares the lock and identifier
functions the Combine module calls, and the archive that defines them is
libCombineHelpers.a. The module map named no library, so a Swift object
that imports Combine recorded -lCombine and nothing for the helpers. A
link that takes its archives from those records then ends with
_opencombine_unfair_lock_*, _opencombine_unfair_recursive_lock_*,
_opencombine_stop_in_debugger and _opencombine_next_combine_identifier
undefined. The link directive makes the module name its own archive, and
the compiler records it with the module.
---
 Sources/COpenCombineHelpers/include/module.modulemap | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Sources/COpenCombineHelpers/include/module.modulemap b/Sources/COpenCombineHelpers/include/module.modulemap
index 2a823a2..bf39104 100644
--- a/Sources/COpenCombineHelpers/include/module.modulemap
+++ b/Sources/COpenCombineHelpers/include/module.modulemap
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
 module COpenCombineHelpers {
   header "COpenCombineHelpers.h"
+  link "CombineHelpers"
 }
